HELM CHART CONFIGURATION GUIDE
=============================

OVERVIEW
--------
This guide documents the Helm chart configuration used for the AI SRE Copilot project.

PROJECT STRUCTURE
-----------------
future-ai-sre-copilot/
|
+-- helm-chart/
    |
    +-- sre-copilot/
        |
        +-- Chart.yaml
        +-- values.yaml
        +-- charts/
        +-- templates/
            |
            +-- deployment.yaml
            +-- service.yaml
            +-- ingress.yaml
            +-- serviceaccount.yaml


STEP 1 - VERIFY CHART STRUCTURE
-------------------------------

# list chart contents
ls -la helm-chart/sre-copilot

Expected:

Chart.yaml
values.yaml
templates/
charts/


STEP 2 - CHART.YAML
-------------------

apiVersion: v2
name: sre-copilot
description: AI SRE Copilot Helm Chart
type: application
version: 0.1.0
appVersion: "1.0"

Explanation:

apiVersion  = Helm chart API version
name        = Chart name
description = Chart description
version     = Chart version
appVersion  = Application version


STEP 3 - VALUES.YAML
--------------------

replicaCount: 1

image:
  repository: hyareldocker1/sre-copilot
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent
  tag: latest

service:
  type: ClusterIP
  port: 8002

Explanation:

replicaCount = Number of pods
repository   = Docker Hub image
pullPolicy   = Image pull strategy
tag          = Image version
port         = Application port


STEP 4 - DEPLOYMENT TEMPLATE
----------------------------

# deployment name
metadata:
  name: sre-copilot

# pod replicas
replicas: 1

# docker image
image: hyareldocker1/sre-copilot:latest

# application port
containerPort: 8002

Explanation:

Deployment manages pods.
containerPort must match FastAPI port.


STEP 5 - SERVICE TEMPLATE
-------------------------

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service

spec:
  type: ClusterIP

  ports:
  - port: 8002
    targetPort: 8002

Explanation:

port       = service port
targetPort = application port


STEP 6 - VALIDATE CHART
-----------------------

# validate helm chart
helm lint ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

Expected:

1 chart(s) linted
0 chart(s) failed


STEP 7 - INSTALL CHART
----------------------

# install helm chart
helm install sre-copilot ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

Expected:

STATUS: deployed


STEP 8 - VERIFY INSTALLATION
----------------------------

# list releases
helm list

# check resources
kubectl get all

# check pods
kubectl get pods


STEP 9 - CHECK RELEASE STATUS
-----------------------------

helm status sre-copilot

Shows:

Deployment
Pods
Services
Release Info


STEP 10 - UPGRADE CHART
-----------------------

# apply chart changes
helm upgrade sre-copilot ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

Purpose:
Update deployment without uninstalling.


STEP 11 - ROLLBACK RELEASE
--------------------------

# show release history
helm history sre-copilot

# rollback version
helm rollback sre-copilot 1

Purpose:
Return to previous working version.


STEP 12 - UNINSTALL CHART
-------------------------

helm uninstall sre-copilot

Purpose:
Remove deployment and Helm release.


USEFUL COMMANDS
---------------

# release list
helm list

# release details
helm status sre-copilot

# release history
helm history sre-copilot

# validate chart
helm lint ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

# install chart
helm install sre-copilot ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

# upgrade chart
helm upgrade sre-copilot ./helm-chart/sre-copilot

# uninstall chart
helm uninstall sre-copilot


HELM WORKFLOW
-------------

Docker Build
      |
Docker Hub
      |
Helm Chart
      |
Helm Install
      |
Kubernetes Deployment
      |
Pod Running


MEMORY FORMULA
--------------
Chart.yaml     = Chart Information
values.yaml    = User Configuration
templates      = Kubernetes Templates
helm lint      = Validate Chart
helm install   = Install Release
helm upgrade   = Upgrade Release
helm rollback  = Restore Release
helm uninstall = Remove Release
